<title>FRANCE: France to offer 16 to 18 bln Ffr of OATs.</title>
<headline>France to offer 16 to 18 bln Ffr of OATs.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>France is to offer between 16 and 18 billion francs of government bonds (OATs) at its next scheduled auction on December 5, the Treasury said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Treasury will offer the current 10-year benchmark OAT, the 6.50 percent October 25, 2006 bond, with a payment date of December 26, a treasury statement said.</p>
<p>The Treasury also said it would offer the 8.25 percent February 27, 2004 OAT and the TEC 10 floating rate bond, both with a payment date of December 26.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
